    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74936" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθο-δίκας</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθοδίκης, ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by which justice is upheld,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶς ὀμφαλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					11.9
				</span></i>
			:—so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθό-δῐκος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, Στύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					10.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				13.23
			</span></i>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθο-δίκαιος</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				994
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
